,"Iteración y mejora","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Sélection d''outils d''IA","Flux de travail de développement","Tests et débogage","Déploiement d''applications","Itération et amélioration","Intégration avec des outils de développement"],"de":["Auswahl von KI-Tools","Entwicklungsworkflow","Tests und Debugging","Bereitstellung von Anwendungen","Iteration und Verbesserung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Seleção de ferramentas de código","Fluxo de trabalho de construção personalizado","Integração com IA para desenvolvimento de aplicativos","Otimização do ciclo de vida de desenvolvimento de software","Suporte para fundadores não técnicos"],"ru":["Выбор инструментов кодирования","Пользовательский рабочий процесс построения","Интеграция с ИИ для разработки приложений","Оптимизация цикла разработки программного обеспечения","Поддержка нетехнических основателей"],"ar":["اختيار أدوات الكود","تدفق عمل بناء مخصص","التكامل مع الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير التطبيقات","تحسين دورة حياة تطوير البرمجيات","دعم المؤسسين غير التقنيين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SaaS应用构建","AI工具","开发工作流","MVP构建","代码优化","自动化测试","非技术创始人","快速开发"],"ja":["SaaSアプリケーションの構築","AIツール","開発ワークフロー","MVPの構築","コードの最適化","自動テスト","非技術的な創業者","迅速な開発"],"ko":["SaaS 애플리케이션 구축","AI 도구","개발 워크플로","MVP 구축","코드 최적화","자동 테스트","비기술 창업자","빠른 개발"],"es":["desarrollo de aplicaciones SaaS","herramientas de IA","ciclo de vida de desarrollo de software","construir aplicaciones","desarrollo de software","SaaS","IA","desarrollo de aplicaciones","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["développement d''applications SaaS","outils d''IA","cycle de vie de développement de logiciels","concevoir des applications","développement de logiciels","SaaS","IA","développement d''applications","outils de développement"],"de":["Entwicklung von SaaS-Anwendungen","KI-Tools","Lebenszyklus der Softwareentwicklung","Erstellen von Anwendungen","Softwareentwicklung","SaaS","KI","Anwendungsentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de aplicativos SaaS","IA para desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de código","ciclo de vida de desenvolvimento de software","fundadores não técnicos","construção de aplicativos com IA"],"ru":["разработка приложений SaaS","ИИ для разработки программного обеспечения","инструменты кодирования","цикл разработки программного обеспечения","нетехнические основатели","построение приложений с ИИ"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات SaaS","الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الكود","دورة حياة تطوير البرمجيات","المؤسسون غير التقنيين","بناء التطبيقات مع الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"whawkinsiv","repo":"solo-founder-superpowers","repoPath":"whawkinsiv/solo-founder-superpowers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.881Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"build","description":"Use this skill when the user needs to build features with AI coding tools, choose between Claude Code, Lovable, Replit, or Cursor, write effective prompts for code generation, or iterate on AI-generated code. Covers tool selection, prompting strategies, and development workflows for non-technical founders.","bodyPreview":"# Build\n\n## Tool Selection\n\n**Starting from scratch?** → Lovable (fastest MVP)  \n**Existing codebase?** → Claude Code (best context)  \n**Learning to code?** → Replit (educational)  \n**Already code?** → Cursor (power features)\n\nSee [TOOLS.md](TOOLS.md) for detailed comparison.\n\n---\n\n## Build Workflow\n\n```\n- [ ] Start with spec (use scope skill)\n- [ ] Give spec to AI tool\n- [ ] Test happy path + edge cases\n- [ ] Give specific feedback on issues\n- [ ] Iterate (expect 2-4 rounds)\n- [ ] Deploy when w","body":"# Build\n\n## Tool Selection\n\n**Starting from scratch?** → Lovable (fastest MVP)  \n**Existing codebase?** → Claude Code (best context)  \n**Learning to code?** → Replit (educational)  \n**Already code?** → Cursor (power features)\n\nSee [TOOLS.md](TOOLS.md) for detailed comparison.\n\n---\n\n## Build Workflow\n\n```\n- [ ] Start with spec (use scope skill)\n- [ ] Give spec to AI tool\n- [ ] Test happy path + edge cases\n- [ ] Give specific feedback on issues\n- [ ] Iterate (expect 2-4 rounds)\n- [ ] Deploy when working\n```\n\n---\n\n## Giving AI Your Spec\n\n### Claude Code\n```\nBuild this feature: [paste spec]\n\nCodebase: React + TypeScript + Tailwind\nReference: src/components/Button.tsx for button patterns\n```\n\n### Lovable\n```\nBuild: [paste simplified spec focusing on outcome]\nMake it look like Linear (minimal, clean)\n```\n\n### Replit\n```\nCreate: [paste spec emphasizing what user sees]\nUse React. Keep simple.\n```\n\nSee [PROMPTS.md](PROMPTS.md) for patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Reviewing What AI Built\n\nTest, don''t just run:\n\n```\n- [ ] Looks right?\n- [ ] Happy path works?\n- [ ] Edge cases work?\n- [ ] Works on mobile?\n- [ ] Error messages clear?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Giving Feedback\n\n**Bad:** \"This doesn''t work\"  \n**Good:** \"Clicking ''Save'' does nothing. Expected: ''Saved!'' message\"\n\n**Template:**\n```\nWhat I tried: [action]\nExpected: [outcome]\nGot: [what happened]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Iteration Expectations\n\n**Normal:** 2-4 rounds per feature  \n**First build:** AI builds from spec, you find 3-5 issues  \n**Second build:** Fixes those, you find 1-2 more  \n**Third build:** Final polish\n\n**Stop when:**\n- Happy path works\n- Edge cases handled\n- Mobile works\n- No obvious bugs\n\n**Don''t iterate for:**\n- Perfection\n- Features beyond spec\n- Premature optimization\n\n---\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| No spec | Use scope skill first |\n| \"Build a dashboard\" | Specify what''s on it |\n| Skip edge case testing | Try breaking it |\n| Accept without review | Always test |\n| Add features mid-build | Finish current feature first |\n| Fix code yourself | Describe problem, let AI fix |\n\n---\n\n## Right-Sizing Work\n\n**Too big:** \"Build entire app\"  \n**Too small:** \"Add one button\"  \n**Right:** \"Build user auth flow\" (1-3 hours)\n\n**Good chunks:**\n- User login/signup flow\n- Dashboard with 4 metrics\n- Settings page with profile editing\n\n---\n\n## When Stuck\n\n**AI keeps breaking things:**\n→ Break into smaller piece, start fresh session\n\n**Can''t figure out complex feature:**\n→ Ask: \"What''s simplest way?\" Accept simpler solution\n\n**Each fix breaks something else:**\n→ Stop. Ask: \"Better approach?\" Consider starting over\n\n---\n\n## Working with Existing Code\n\n```\nAdd [feature] to existing project.\n\nStack: [React, Next.js, etc]\nPatterns: Check src/components for examples\nStyle: Tailwind + custom design system\nFollow existing code style\n```\n\n---\n\n## Prompting Patterns\n\n**Reference existing:**\n```\nBuild Settings page.\nReference Dashboard page layout.\nUse same Card/Button components.\n```\n\n**Provide examples:**\n```\nPricing page with 3 tiers.\nLike Linear''s pricing - clean, minimal.\n```\n\n**Specify constraints:**\n```\nBuild profile page.\nMust work offline.\nLoad under 2 seconds.\nWCAG AA accessible.\n```\n\nSee [PROMPTS.md](PROMPTS.md) for more.\n\n---\n\n## Review for Non-Technical Founders\n\n**Check:**\n- Does it match spec?\n- Buttons work?\n- Forms validate?\n- Looks like design reference?\n- Works on mobile?\n- Error messages clear?\n\n**Don''t check:**\n- Code cleanliness\n- Optimization\n- \"Best practices\"\n\nAI handles code quality. You handle requirements.\n\n---\n\n## Success Looks Like\n\n✅ Features match specs  \n✅ 2-4 iterations (not 10+)  \n✅ Can explain what''s wrong  \n✅ Building faster each week\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:08:15.270Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing streamlined software development lifecycle management for SaaS applications","zh":"适用于 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等 AI 代理，需要简化的软件开发生命周期管理，用于 SaaS 应用程序","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの AI エージェントに適しており、SaaS アプリケーション向けのストリームライン化されたソフトウェア開発ライフサイクル管理が必要","ko":"Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, SaaS 애플리케이션을 위한简化된 소프트웨어 개발 생명주기 관리가 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan una gestión del ciclo de vida de desarrollo de software optimizada para aplicaciones SaaS","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain ayant besoin d''une gestion du cycle de vie de développement de logiciels rationalisée pour les applications SaaS","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine optimierte Software-Entwicklungslebenszyklusverwaltung für SaaS-Anwendungen benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de gestão do ciclo de vida de desenvolvimento de software simplificada para aplicações SaaS","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которым требуется упрощенное управление жизненным циклом разработки программного обеспечения для приложений SaaS","ar":"مثالية لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة دورة حياة تطوير البرمجيات المبسطة للتطبيقات السحابية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage tools like Lovable, Replit, and Cursor for rapid MVP development, educational coding, and power feature implementation, streamlining the build workflow with spec-driven development, AI tool integration, and iterative testing using protocols like happy path and edge case analysis","zh":"赋予代理使用 Lovable、Replit 和 Cursor 等工具进行快速 MVP 开发、教育编码和功能实现，通过使用规范驱动开发、AI 工具集成和迭代测试等方式简化构建工作流，并使用诸如 happy path 和边缘情况分析等协议","ja":"Lovable、Replit、Cursor などのツールを使用して、迅速な MVP 開発、教育コーディング、機能実装を可能にし、ビルド ワークフローをストリームライン化するために、仕様駆動開発、AI ツール統合、反復テストなどの方法を使用し、happy path やエッジ ケース分析などのプロトコルを使用","ko":"Lovable, Replit, Cursor 등의 도구를 사용하여 빠른 MVP 개발, 교육 코딩, 기능 구현을 가능하게 하며, 빌드 워크플로우를簡化하기 위해 규격 주도 개발, AI 도구 통합, 반복 테스트 등의 방법을 사용하고, happy path 또는 에지 케이스 분석 등의 프로토콜을 사용","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar herramientas como Lovable, Replit y Cursor para un desarrollo de MVP rápido, codificación educativa y implementación de características potentes, racionalizando el flujo de trabajo de compilación con desarrollo basado en especificaciones, integración de herramientas de IA y pruebas iterativas utilizando protocolos como análisis de ruta feliz y caso límite","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser des outils comme Lovable, Replit et Cursor pour un développement de MVP rapide, une codification éducative et une mise en œuvre de fonctionnalités puissantes, en rationalisant le flux de travail de construction avec un développement basé sur des spécifications, une intégration d''outils d''IA et des tests itératifs en utilisant des protocoles tels que l''analyse de chemin heureux et d''analyse de cas limite","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Tools wie Lovable, Replit und Cursor für eine schnelle MVP-Entwicklung, Bildungscoding und leistungsstarke Funktionsimplementierung zu nutzen, indem sie den Build-Workflow mit spezifikationsgetriebenem Entwicklungsprozess, KI-Tool-Integration und iterativem Testen unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie Happy-Path- und Edge-Case-Analyse rationalisieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar ferramentas como Lovable, Replit e Cursor para desenvolvimento rápido de MVP, codificação educacional e implementação de recursos poderosos, simplificando o fluxo de trabalho de compilação com desenvolvimento orientado por especificações, integração de ferramentas de IA e teste iterativo usando protocolos como análise de caminho feliz e caso de bordo","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать инструменты, такие как Lovable, Replit и Cursor, для быстрой разработки MVP, образовательного кодирования и реализации мощных функций, оптимизируя рабочий процесс сборки с помощью разработки, управляемой спецификациями, интеграции инструментов ИИ и итеративного тестирования с использованием протоколов, таких как анализ счастливого пути и краевого случая","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من أدوات مثل Lovable و Replit و Cursor من أجل تطوير MVP سريع والبرمجة التعليمية وتنفيذ ميزات قوية، وبذلك تُبسط تدفق العمل لبناء البرمجيات باستخدام تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات وتكامل أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي والاختبار التكراري باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل تحليل المسار السعيد و تحليل الحالات الحدودية"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating SaaS application builds with Lovable","Debugging existing codebases with Claude Code","Generating educational coding environments with Replit"],"zh":["使用 Lovable 自动化 SaaS 应用程序构建","使用 Claude Code 调试现有代码库","使用 Replit 生成教育编码环境"],"ja":["Lovable を使用して SaaS アプリケーションのビルドを自動化する","Claude Code を使用して既存のコードベースをデバッグする","Replit を使用して教育コーディング環境を生成する"],"ko":["Lovable을 사용하여 SaaS 애플리케이션 빌드를 자동화","Claude Code를 사용하여 기존 코드베이스를 디버깅","Replit을 사용하여 교육 코딩 환경을 생성"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de aplicaciones SaaS con Lovable","Depuración de código existente con Claude Code","Generación de entornos de codificación educativa con Replit"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création d''applications SaaS avec Lovable","Débogage de codebases existantes avec Claude Code","Génération d''environnements de codage éducatif avec Replit"],"de":["Automatisierung von SaaS-Anwendungsbuilds mit Lovable","Fehlerbehebung in bestehenden Codebasen mit Claude Code","Erzeugung von Bildungscoding-Umgebungen mit Replit"],"pt":["Automatizar compilações de aplicações SaaS com Lovable","Depurar código existente com Claude Code","Gerar ambientes de codificação educacional com Replit"],"ru":["Автоматизировать сборку приложений SaaS с помощью Lovable","Отлаживать существующий код с помощью Claude Code","Генерировать образовательные среды кодирования с помощью Replit"],"ar":["تأتمتة بناء تطبيقات السحابة باستخدام Lovable","تصحيح أخطاء الكود الموجود باستخدام Claude Code","إنشاء بيئات برمجة تعليمية باستخدام Replit"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires AI tool access like Lovable, Replit, or Claude Code","Limited to SaaS application development"],"zh":["需要访问 AI 工具，如 Lovable、Replit 或 Claude Code","仅限 SaaS 应用程序开发"],"ja":["Lovable、Replit、または Claude Code などの AI ツールへのアクセスが必要","SaaS アプリケーション開発に限定"],"ko":["Lovable, Replit, Claude Code 등의 AI 도구 액세스가 필요","SaaS 애플리케이션 개발에 한정"],"es":["Requiere acceso a herramientas de IA como Lovable, Replit o Claude Code","Limitado a la desarrollo de aplicaciones SaaS"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des outils d''IA comme Lovable, Replit ou Claude Code","Limité au développement d''applications SaaS"],"de":["Benötigt Zugang zu KI-Tools wie Lovable, Replit oder Claude Code","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von SaaS-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Exige acesso a ferramentas de IA como Lovable, Replit ou Claude Code","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de aplicações SaaS"],"ru":["Требует доступа к инструментам ИИ, таким как Lovable, Replit или Claude Code","Ограничен разработкой приложений SaaS"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Lovable و Replit و Claude Code","محدود بتطوير تطبيقات السحابة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0c1f4469b5c1138e2f9e9bf2445362fb0efc9a284f0e2f9b2990521cf056e5f6","qualityScore":36}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('SudoMaker/rEFui/refui', 'community', 'SudoMaker', 'rEFui', 'SudoMaker/rEFui', 'refui', 0, 0, 36, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.881Z', '2026-03-02T02:08:29.679Z', '82cd8194aa22335e8918571d0ce03ff2f0614eaa901a783a6cc09c3be82640eb', '{"id":"SudoMaker/rEFui/refui","name":"refui","description":{"zh":"Refui是一个JavaScript框架，用于构建跨 web、native 和嵌入式UI项目，提高开发效率","ja":"Refuiは、Web、ネイティブ、埋め込みUIプロジェクトを構築するためのJavaScriptフレームワークです","ko":"Refui는 웹, 네이티브, 임베디드 UI 프로젝트를 구축하기 위한 JavaScript 프레임워크입니다","es":"Refui es un framework JavaScript que acelera el desarrollo de proyectos UI en diferentes plataformas. Ofrece una solución integral para crear interfaces de usuario innovadoras","fr":"Refui est un framework JavaScript qui accélère le développement de projets UI sur différentes plateformes. Il offre une solution complète pour créer des interfaces utilisateur innovantes","de":"Refui ist ein JavaScript-Framework, das die Entwicklung von UI-Projekten auf verschiedenen Plattformen beschleunigt. Es bietet eine umfassende Lösung zur Erstellung von innovativen Benutzeroberflächen","pt":"Refui é um framework JavaScript que facilita a criação de projetos de UI em web, nativo e embarcado","ru":"Refui - это фреймворк JavaScript, который упрощает разработку проектов UI для веба, натива и встраиваемых систем","ar":"Refui هو إطار عمل JavaScript يسهل إنشاء مشاريع واجهة المستخدم على الويب والأصلية والمضمنة","en":"The JavaScript framework that refuels your UI projects, across web, native, and embedded"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Refui：AI智能UI框架","ja":"Refui：AIエージェントによるUIフレームワーク","ko":"Refui: AI 에이전트 기반 UI 프레임워크","es":"Refui: Framework JavaScript para UI","fr":"Refui: Le framework JavaScript pour les projets UI","de":"Refui: JavaScript-Framework für UI-Projekte","pt":"Refui: Ferramenta de UI para Web, Nativo e Embarcado","ru":"Refui: Инструмент для UI веб, натива и встраиваемых проектов","ar":"Refui: أداة واجهة المستخدم للويب والأصلية والمضمنة","en":"refui"},"description":{"zh":"Refui是一个JavaScript框架，用于构建跨 web、native 和嵌入式UI项目，提高开发效率","ja":"Refuiは、Web、ネイティブ、埋め込みUIプロジェクトを構築するためのJavaScriptフレームワークです","ko":"Refui는 웹, 네이티브, 임베디드 UI 프로젝트를 구축하기 위한 JavaScript 프레임워크입니다","es":"Refui es un framework JavaScript que acelera el desarrollo de proyectos UI en diferentes plataformas. Ofrece una solución integral para crear interfaces de u...","fr":"Refui est un framework JavaScript qui accélère le développement de projets UI sur différentes plateformes. Il offre une solution complète pour créer des inte...","de":"Refui ist ein JavaScript-Framework, das die Entwicklung von UI-Projekten auf verschiedenen Plattformen beschleunigt. Es bietet eine umfassende Lösung zur Ers...","pt":"Refui é um framework JavaScript que facilita a criação de projetos de UI em web, nativo e embarcado","ru":"Refui - это фреймворк JavaScript, который упрощает разработку проектов UI для веба, натива и встраиваемых систем","ar":"Refui هو إطار عمل JavaScript يسهل إنشاء مشاريع واجهة المستخدم على الويب والأصلية والمضمنة","en":"The JavaScript framework that refuels your UI projects, across web, native, and embedded"},"definition":{"en":"The JavaScript framework that refuels your UI projects, across web, native, and embedded"},"features":{"zh":["跨平台支持","高效的UI开发","简单易用的API","支持Web、native和嵌入式UI项目","提高开发效率"],"ja":["クロスプラットフォーム対応","効率的なUI開発","シンプルで使いやすいAPI","Web、ネイティブ、埋め込みUIプロジェクト対応","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["크로스 플랫폼 지원","효율적인 UI 개발","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 API","웹, 네이티브, 임베디드 UI 프로젝트 지원","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Desarrollo de interfaces de usuario personalizadas","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas","Escalabilidad y flexibilidad","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo populares","Documentación y soporte comunitario"],"fr":["Développement d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes","Évolutivité et flexibilité","Intégration avec des outils de développement populaires","Documentation et support communautaire"],"de":["Entwicklung benutzerdefinierter Benutzeroberflächen","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen","Skalierbarkeit und Flexibilität","Integration mit beliebten Entwicklungstools","Dokumentation und Community-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de UI personalizado","Compatibilidade com web, nativo e embarcado","Framework JavaScript leve e flexível","Fácil integração com outras bibliotecas","Suporte a múltiplos ambientes de execução"],"ru":["Настройка интерфейса пользователя","Совместимость с вебом, натива и встраиваемыми системами","Легкий и гибкий фреймворк JavaScript","Легкая интеграция с другими библиотеками","Поддержка нескольких сред выполнения"],"ar":["تطوير واجهة المستخدم المخصصة","التوافق مع الويب والأصلية والمضمنة","إطار عمل JavaScript خفيف ومﾄlexible","التكامل السهل مع المكتبات الأخرى","دعم بيئات تشغيل متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Refui","AI智能UI框架","JavaScript框架","UI开发","跨平台支持","如何使用Refui","Refui安装","Refui设置指南"],"ja":["Refui","AIエージェントによるUIフレームワーク","JavaScriptフレームワーク","UI開発","クロスプラットフォーム対応","Refuiの使い方","Refuiのインストール","Refuiの設定ガイド"],"ko":["Refui","AI 에이전트 기반 UI 프레임워크","JavaScript 프레임워크","UI 개발","크로스 플랫폼 지원","Refui 사용법","Refui 설치","Refui 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de desarrollo web","frameworks JavaScript","desarrollo de interfaces de usuario","Refui vs React","cómo usar Refui","guía de instalación de Refui","alternativas a Refui"],"fr":["outils de développement web","frameworks JavaScript","développement d''interfaces utilisateur","Refui vs React","comment utiliser Refui","guide d''installation de Refui","alternatives à Refui"],"de":["Web-Entwicklungstools","JavaScript-Frameworks","Entwicklung von Benutzeroberflächen","Refui vs React","wie man Refui verwendet","Refui-Installationsanleitung","Alternativen zu Refui"],"pt":["refui","framework ui","desenvolvimento de ui","javascript","web","nativo","embarcado","como usar refui","o que é refui"],"ru":["refui","фреймворк ui","разработка ui","javascript","веб","натива","встраиваемые системы","как использовать refui","что такое refui"],"ar":["refui","إطار عمل واجهة المستخدم","تطوير واجهة المستخدم","javascript","الويب","الأصلية","المضمنة","كيفية استخدام refui","ما هو refui"]}},"owner":"SudoMaker","repo":"rEFui","repoPath":"SudoMaker/rEFui","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.881Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"refui","description":"Use when working with rEFui (refui) applications where you cannot rely on reading the library source. Covers the retained-mode + signals mental model, DOM/HTML/Reflow renderers, JSX setup (classic pragma vs automatic runtime), directives (on:/class:/style:/attr:/prop:/m: macros), HMR via refurbish/refui/hmr, debugging “UI not updating” issues, and migrating React/Vue/Solid/Svelte patterns to rEFui.","bodyPreview":"# rEFui\n\n## Overview\n\nApply rEFui’s retained-mode + signals model correctly, choose the right JSX mode/renderer, and fix reactivity/lifecycle issues without importing patterns from other UI frameworks.\n\n## General guide\n\n### Mental model (retained mode)\n\n- Component bodies are **setup**: they run once; they do not “re-render”.\n- JSX is evaluated once; **signals** update the already-built UI incrementally.\n- If something “doesn’t update”, you almost always read `.value` too early (non-reactively)","body":"# rEFui\n\n## Overview\n\nApply rEFui’s retained-mode + signals model correctly, choose the right JSX mode/renderer, and fix reactivity/lifecycle issues without importing patterns from other UI frameworks.\n\n## General guide\n\n### Mental model (retained mode)\n\n- Component bodies are **setup**: they run once; they do not “re-render”.\n- JSX is evaluated once; **signals** update the already-built UI incrementally.\n- If something “doesn’t update”, you almost always read `.value` too early (non-reactively) or mutated in place without `trigger()`.\n\n### Signals & reactivity\n\n- State: `const count = signal(0)`\n- Reactive JSX: `{count}` (not `{count.value}`)\n- Derived: `const label = $(() => `Count: ${count.value}`)` and then `{label}`\n- In-place mutation: call `sig.trigger()` after mutating arrays/objects.\n\n```jsx\nimport { signal, $ } from ''refui''\n\nconst Counter = () => {\n\tconst count = signal(0)\n\treturn (\n\t\t<button on:click={() => count.set(count.value + 1)}>\n\t\t\t{$(() => `Count: ${count.value}`)}\n\t\t</button>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n### Effects & cleanup\n\n- Reactive effect: `watch(() => { ...reads signals... })`\n- Setup/cleanup: `useEffect(() => { ...; return () => cleanup })`\n- Teardown-only: `onDispose(() => cleanup)`\n- Scheduling: if you need “after updates applied”, `await nextTick()`.\n\n### Control flow components\n\n- Conditional UI: `<If condition={cond}>{() => <Then />}{() => <Else />}</If>`\n- Lists: `<For entries={items} track=\"id\">{({ item, index }) => ...}</For>`\n- Inline dynamic subtree with lifecycle: `<Fn ctx={something}>{(ctx) => ...}</Fn>`\n- `For` has **no** `fallback`; for empty states, wrap with `<If>`.\n\n```jsx\nimport { signal, $, If, For } from ''refui''\n\nconst App = () => {\n\tconst items = signal([{ id: 1, name: ''A'' }])\n\treturn (\n\t\t<If condition={$(() => items.value.length)}>\n\t\t\t{() => <For entries={items} track=\"id\">{({ item }) => <div>{item.name}</div>}</For>}\n\t\t\t{() => <div>Empty</div>}\n\t\t</If>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n### Async UI\n\n- `<Async>` for a single promise boundary.\n- `<Suspense>` to group multiple async subtrees under one fallback.\n- `lazy(() => import(...))` for code-splitting; pair with fallback boundaries.\nSee `references/async-suspense-transition.md` for the “rules of engagement”.\n\n### Context\n\nUse context for shared subtree values. If consumers must react to changes, provide a signal as the context value.\n\n```jsx\nimport { signal, $, createContext, useContext } from ''refui''\n\nconst Theme = createContext(signal(''light''), ''Theme'')\n\nconst Button = () => {\n\tconst theme = useContext(Theme)\n\treturn <button class:dark={$(() => theme.value === ''dark'')}>OK</button>\n}\n```\n\nNon-Reflow/custom renderer: wrap Provider children in a function so they inherit context: `<Theme value={x}>{() => <Button />}</Theme>`.\n\n### Mounting (DOM / HTML)\n\n- DOM renderer (browser): `createDOMRenderer(defaults).render(target, App)`\n- HTML renderer (SSR/SSG): `createHTMLRenderer().serialize(createElement(App, props))`\n- JSX + renderer selection: see `references/jsx-and-renderers.md` (automatic vs classic transform).\n\n```jsx\nimport { createDOMRenderer } from ''refui/dom''\nimport { defaults } from ''refui/browser''\n\ncreateDOMRenderer(defaults).render(document.getElementById(''app''), App)\n```\n\n### DOM directives (browser preset)\n\n- Events: `on:click={fn}` (+ `on-once:*`, `on-passive:*`, `on-capture:*`)\n- Classes/styles: `class:active={boolOrSignal}`, `style:color={valueOrSignal}`\n- Attributes vs props: `attr:*` (SVG/read-only), `prop:*` (force property write)\n- Macros: `m:*` for reusable DOM behaviors (renderer-registered handlers)\n\n## Default Policy: Use rEFui Built-ins First\n\nWhen implementing a requirement, prefer rEFui’s built-in primitives (signals/components/extras/renderers) over custom plumbing. Only fall back to a custom implementation when:\n- rEFui has no built-in primitive that matches the requirement, and\n- the project’s rEFui version lacks an equivalent helper, and\n- you can’t express it cleanly as a DOM macro (`m:*`) or small reusable component.\n\nBefore writing code, consult `references/dos-and-donts.md` to avoid React-style mistakes.\n\n## Quick Triage (do this first)\n\n1. Identify **JSX mode** in the target repo:\n\t - **Automatic runtime**: look for `jsx: ''automatic''` + `jsxImportSource: ''refui''` (Vite/esbuild) or `jsxImportSource: \"refui\"` (tsconfig/Bun).\n\t - **Classic transform**: look for `jsxFactory: ''R.c''` + `jsxFragment: ''R.f''` (Vite/esbuild) or `/** @jsx R.c */` file pragmas.\n2. Identify the **host renderer**:\n\t - Browser apps: `createDOMRenderer(defaults)` from `refui/dom` + `refui/browser` (or `refui/presets/browser` in older repos).\n\t - SSR/SSG: `createHTMLRenderer()` from `refui/html`, then `serialize()`.\n\t - Reflow logic-only modules: `refui/reflow` (often injected via `jsxInject: import { R } from ''refui/reflow''` in classic mode).\n3. Confirm **rEFui version** (it changes API details across repos). Prefer the repo’s local docs or installed `refui` exports.\n\nIf you want an automated scan for JSX mode + common pitfalls, run `node scripts/refui-audit.mjs <path>` from inside this skill folder.\n\n## When Usage Is Unclear (consult MCP docs)\n\nIf you are unsure about a rEFui API, behavior, or best practice and cannot inspect the library source:\n\n- Use **Context7 MCP** to pull authoritative, up-to-date library docs/snippets:\n\t- First resolve the library: `mcp__context7__resolve-library-id` with `libraryName: \"refui\"`.\n\t- Then query: `mcp__context7__query-docs` for the specific API/task (e.g. “`For` track vs indexed”, “`createDOMRenderer` macros”, “`nextTick` vs `tick` semantics”, “classic vs automatic JSX setup”).\n- Use **DeepWiki MCP** for repository-level questions (when the upstream repo is available):\n\t- `mcp__deepwiki__read_wiki_structure` then `mcp__deepwiki__ask_question` on `SudoMaker/rEFui` for conceptual/system questions or “where is X documented?”.\n\nIf MCP docs still leave ambiguity, ask the user for: the `refui` version, their bundler config (Vite/esbuild/Bun/TS/Babel), and a minimal repro snippet.\n\n## “Which rEFui feature should I use?” (fast mapping)\n\nUse these references when choosing a built-in solution:\n- Idiot-proof do/don’t checklist: `references/dos-and-donts.md`\n- Async UI: `references/async-suspense-transition.md`\n- Overlays/teleports/rich HTML/custom elements: `references/portals-parse-custom-elements.md`\n- Lists/identity/caching/perf: `references/lists-cache-memo.md`\n- Project setup: `references/project-setup.md`\n\n## Non-Negotiables (retained mode)\n\n- Do not write React/Vue/Solid/Svelte primitives (`useState`, hooks, VDOM assumptions, `$:` blocks, etc.). Map them to rEFui signals/effects.\n- Treat component bodies as **setup** (constructor-ish). JSX is evaluated once; signals drive incremental updates afterward.\n- Keep reactive reads reactive:\n\t- ✅ Use a signal directly: `<div>{count}</div>`\n\t- ✅ Wrap derived expressions: `<div>{$(() => `Count: ${count.value}`)}</div>` or `<div>{computed(() => ...)}</div>`\n\t- ❌ Avoid inline `.value` in JSX: `<div>{count.value}</div>` (evaluates once, won’t update)\n- Remember scheduling: signal effects/computed flush at the end of the tick; use `await nextTick()` when you must observe derived updates.\n\n## Hard Rules (idiot-proof guardrails)\n\n- This is **not React**. Component bodies run once; JSX does not re-run. Do not expect re-renders.\n- Do not invent props. If the API is unclear, open the .d.ts or use MCP. Example: `For` has **no** `fallback` prop.\n- `If` / `For` / templates accept a **single** renderable. If you need multiple nodes, wrap them in a container or fragment.\n- `For` empty state: wrap it in `If` and provide a false branch. Example:\n\t- `<If condition={$(() => items.value.length)}><For entries={items} track=\"id\">{({ item }) => <Row item={item} />}</For><Empty /></If>`\n- Use `.value` inside `computed` / `$(() => ...)` / `watch` / event handlers, not directly in JSX text/attrs.\n\n## Default Patterns (copy these mentally)\n\n- State: `const x = signal(initial)`\n- Derived: `const y = $(() => /* uses x.value */)` (or `computed(() => ...)`)\n- Effects: `watch(fn)` for reactive computations; `useEffect(setup)` for setup+cleanup; `onDispose(cleanup)` for teardown.\n- Lists:\n\t- Keyed: `<For entries={items} track=\"id\">{({ item }) => ...}</For>`\n\t- Unkeyed (perf experiments / reorder heavy): `UnKeyed` from `refui/extras/unkeyed.js`\n\t- If mutating arrays/objects in place: call `sig.trigger()` after mutation.\n- Async:\n\t- `<Async future={promise} fallback={...} catch={...}>{({ result }) => ...}</Async>`\n\t- `<Suspense>` for grouping async subtrees\n\t- `async` components are supported; pair with fallbacks when needed.\n- DOM directives/events (DOM renderer):\n\t- Events: `on:click={...}`, plus options `on-once:*`, `on-passive:*`, `on-capture:*`\n\t- Attributes vs props: prefer `attr:` for SVG or when a DOM prop is read-only; use `prop:` to force a property set.\n\t- Preset directives (browser preset): `class:x={boolSignal}`, `style:color={valueOrSignal}`\n\t- Macros: `m:name={value}` where `name` is registered on the renderer.\n- Refs/handles:\n\t- `$ref={sig}` to receive a node/instance in `sig.value`\n\t- `$ref={(node) => ...}` callback form\n\t- Prefer `expose` prop for imperative child handles (v0.8.0+).\n\n## Workflows\n\n### Fix “UI not updating”\n\n1. Search for JSX `{something.value}` and decide if it must be reactive:\n\t - Replace with `{something}` when `something` is already a signal.\n\t - Wrap derived text/attrs with `$(() => ...)` / `computed(() => ...)` / `t\\`...\\``.\n2. If you mutated an object/array held by a signal in-place, add `sig.trigger()` (or replace with a new object/array).\n3. If you read derived values immediately after writes, insert `await nextTick()` before reading computed/DOM-dependent values.\n4. If an effect runs “forever”, ensure it’s created inside a component scope and cleaned up via `useEffect`/`onDispose`.\n\n### Add a feature safely\n\n1. Keep renderer creation at the entry point; do not create renderers inside components.\n2. Localize state: prefer per-component signals over global blobs; use `extract`/`derivedExtract` to reduce fan-out.\n3. For repeated DOM behaviors, register a macro and use it via `m:*` rather than duplicating manual DOM code.\n4. For lists, choose keyed `<For>` unless you have a measured reason to use unkeyed.\n\n### Set up a new project (when asked)\n\n1. Ask only: preferred package manager (`npm`/`pnpm`/`yarn`/`bun`) and language (JS/TS). Do not ask runtime.\n2. Default to JSX automatic runtime + JavaScript + `refui` latest from npm unless the user specifies otherwise.\n3. Follow `references/project-setup.md`.\n\n## Repo Navigation (load only if needed)\n\nRead these files when you need deeper details:\n\n- `references/project-triage.md` for determining JSX mode/renderer/version from a project that uses rEFui as a dependency.\n- `references/project-setup.md` for scaffolding a new project (default: JSX automatic runtime + pure JS).\n- `references/jsx-and-renderers.md` for choosing classic vs automatic and DOM/HTML/Reflow specifics.\n- `references/reactivity-pitfalls.md` for high-signal debugging checklists and anti-patterns.\n- `references/dos-and-donts.md` for per-API/component do’s and don’ts that prevent React-mindset mistakes.\n- `references/async-suspense-transition.md` for `<Async>`, `<Suspense>`, `lazy`, and `Transition`.\n- `references/portals-parse-custom-elements.md` for portals/teleports, HTML parsing, and custom elements.\n- `references/lists-cache-memo.md` for `<For>`, identity, `UnKeyed`, caching, and memoization.\n\n## Resources\n\n### `scripts/`\n- `scripts/refui-audit.mjs`: quick scan for JSX mode + common `.value`-in-JSX pitfalls.\n\n### `references/`\n- `references/project-triage.md`\n- `references/jsx-and-renderers.md`\n- `references/reactivity-pitfalls.md`\n- `references/dos-and-donts.md`\n- `references/async-suspense-transition.md`\n- `references/portals-parse-custom-elements.md`\n- `references/lists-cache-memo.md`\n- `references/project-setup.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:08:29.679Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents requiring efficient UI development with retained-mode and signals model","zh":"适用于需要高效UI开发并保留模式和信号模型的前端代理","ja":"効率的なUI開発と保留モードおよびシグナルモデルを必要とするフロントエンドエージェントに最適","ko":"효율적인 UI 개발과 유지 모드 및 신호 모델을 필요로 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend que requieren un desarrollo de UI