me","kryptographischer Konsens","parallele Tests","LLMs","erweiterte Sicherheit","Installation von KI-Tools","Sicherheitskonfigurationsanleitung"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é Lamport Distributed Systems","ferramentas de IA para segurança","Lamport Distributed Systems alternativa","Lamport Distributed Systems vs outros","instalar Lamport Distributed Systems","guia de configuração do Lamport Distributed Systems"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое ИИ Агенты: Lamport Distributed Systems","ИИ Агенты для безопасности","ИИ Агенты: Lamport Distributed Systems альтернатива","ИИ Агенты: Lamport Distributed Systems vs другие","установить ИИ Агенты: Lamport Distributed Systems","руководство по настройке ИИ Агентов: Lamport Distributed Systems"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو نظام لامبورت الموزع","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لأمن المعلومات","نظام لامبورت الموزع بديل","نظام لامبورت الموزع مقابل المنافسين","تثبيت نظام لامبورت الموزع","دليل إعداد نظام لامبورت الموزع"]}},"owner":"copyleftdev","repo":"blsmesh","repoPath":"copyleftdev/blsmesh","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.912Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"lamport-distributed-systems","description":"Design distributed systems using Leslie Lamports rigorous approach. Emphasizes formal reasoning, logical time, consensus protocols, and state machine replication. Use when building systems where correctness under concurrency and partial failure is critical.","bodyPreview":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"","body":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"If you''re thinking without writing, you only think you''re thinking.\"\n\n> \"The way to be a good programmer is to write programs, not to learn languages.\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Formal Specification First**: Write a precise specification before writing code. If you can''t specify it precisely, you don''t understand it.\n\n2. **Time is Relative**: There is no global clock in a distributed system. Use logical time (happens-before) to reason about ordering.\n\n3. **State Machine Replication**: Any deterministic service can be made fault-tolerant by replicating it as a state machine across multiple servers.\n\n4. **Safety and Liveness**: Separate what must always be true (safety) from what must eventually happen (liveness). Prove both.\n\n5. **Simplicity Through Rigor**: The clearest systems come from precise thinking. Formalism isn''t overhead—it''s the path to simplicity.\n\n## When Designing Systems\n\n### Always\n\n- Write a specification before implementation (TLA+, Alloy, or precise prose)\n- Define the safety properties: what bad things must never happen\n- Define the liveness properties: what good things must eventually happen\n- Reason about all possible interleavings of concurrent operations\n- Use logical timestamps when physical time isn''t reliable\n- Make system state explicit and transitions clear\n- Document invariants that must hold across all states\n\n### Never\n\n- Assume messages arrive in order (unless you''ve proven it)\n- Assume clocks are synchronized (they''re not)\n- Assume failures are independent (they''re often correlated)\n- Hand-wave about \"eventually\" without defining what guarantees that\n- Trust intuition for concurrent systems—prove it or test it exhaustively\n- Confuse the specification with the implementation\n\n### Prefer\n\n- State machines over ad-hoc event handling\n- Logical clocks over physical timestamps for ordering\n- Consensus protocols over optimistic concurrency for critical state\n- Explicit failure handling over implicit assumptions\n- Proved algorithms over clever heuristics\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Logical Clocks (Lamport Timestamps)\n\n```\nEach process maintains a counter C:\n1. Before any event, increment C\n2. When sending a message, include C\n3. When receiving a message with timestamp T, set C = max(C, T) + 1\n\nThis gives a partial ordering: if a → b, then C(a) < C(b)\n(But C(a) < C(b) does NOT imply a → b)\n```\n\n### The Happens-Before Relation (→)\n\n```\na → b (a happens before b) if:\n1. a and b are in the same process and a comes before b, OR\n2. a is a send and b is the corresponding receive, OR\n3. There exists c such that a → c and c → b (transitivity)\n\nIf neither a → b nor b → a, events are CONCURRENT.\n```\n\n### State Machine Replication\n\n```\nTo replicate a service:\n1. Model the service as a deterministic state machine\n2. Replicate the state machine across N servers\n3. Use consensus (Paxos/Raft) to agree on the sequence of inputs\n4. Each replica applies inputs in the same order → same state\n\nTolerates F failures with 2F+1 replicas.\n```\n\n### Paxos (Simplified)\n\n```\nThree roles: Proposers, Acceptors, Learners\n\nPhase 1 (Prepare):\n  Proposer sends PREPARE(n) to acceptors\n  Acceptor responds with highest-numbered proposal it accepted (if any)\n  \nPhase 2 (Accept):\n  If proposer receives majority responses:\n    Send ACCEPT(n, v) where v is highest-numbered value seen (or new value)\n  Acceptor accepts if it hasn''t promised to a higher proposal\n\nConsensus reached when majority accept the same (n, v).\n```\n\n## Mental Model\n\nLamport approaches distributed systems as a mathematician:\n\n1. **Define the problem precisely**: What are the inputs, outputs, and allowed behaviors?\n2. **Identify the invariants**: What must always be true?\n3. **Consider all interleavings**: What happens if events occur in any order?\n4. **Prove correctness**: Show that safety and liveness hold.\n5. **Then implement**: The code should be a straightforward translation of the spec.\n\n### The TLA+ Approach\n\n```\n1. Define the state space (all possible states)\n2. Define the initial state predicate\n3. Define the next-state relation (allowed transitions)\n4. Specify safety as invariants (always true)\n5. Specify liveness as temporal properties (eventually true)\n6. Model-check or prove that the spec satisfies properties\n```\n\n## Code Patterns\n\n### Implementing Logical Clocks\n\n```python\nclass LamportClock:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._time = 0\n    \n    def tick(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Increment before local event.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def send_timestamp(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get timestamp for outgoing message.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def receive(self, msg_timestamp: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Update clock on message receipt.\"\"\"\n        self._time = max(self._time, msg_timestamp) + 1\n        return self._time\n```\n\n### Vector Clocks (for Causality Detection)\n\n```python\nclass VectorClock:\n    def __init__(self, node_id: str, num_nodes: int):\n        self._id = node_id\n        self._clock = {f\"node_{i}\": 0 for i in range(num_nodes)}\n    \n    def tick(self):\n        self._clock[self._id] += 1\n    \n    def send(self) -> dict:\n        self.tick()\n        return self._clock.copy()\n    \n    def receive(self, other: dict):\n        for node, time in other.items():\n            self._clock[node] = max(self._clock.get(node, 0), time)\n        self.tick()\n    \n    def happens_before(self, other: dict) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if self → other.\"\"\"\n        return all(self._clock[k] <= other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock) \\\n           and any(self._clock[k] < other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock)\n```\n\n## Warning Signs\n\nYou''re violating Lamport''s principles if:\n\n- You assume \"this will never happen in practice\" without proof\n- Your distributed algorithm works \"most of the time\"\n- You can''t write down the invariants your system maintains\n- You''re using wall-clock time for ordering in a distributed system\n- You haven''t considered what happens during network partitions\n- Your system has no formal specification\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- For detailed philosophy, see [philosophy.md](philosophy.md)\n- For references (papers, talks), see [references.md](references.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:21:57.487Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Distributed System Agents needing robust consensus protocols and logical clock implementations.","zh":"适用于需要强大一致性协议和逻辑时钟实现的分布式系统代理。","ja":"分散システムエージェントが堅牢なコンセンサスプロトコルと論理時計実装を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"분산 시스템 에이전트가 강력한 합의 프로토콜과 논리 시계 구현을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de sistemas distribuidos que necesitan protocolos de consenso robustos e implementaciones de relojes lógicos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant des protocoles de consensus robustes et des implémentations d''horloges logiques.","de":"Perfekt für Agenten in verteilten Systemen, die robuste Konsensprotokolle und Implementierungen logischer Uhren benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que necessitam de protocolos de consenso robustos e implementações de relógios lógicos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов распределенных систем, требующих надежных протоколов согласования и реализаций логических часов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء أنظمة الموزعة التي تحتاج إلى بروتوكولات إجماع قوية وتنفيذات ساعات منطقية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and evaluate distributed systems using Paxos consensus and TLA+ formal specification, ensuring reliable and secure data exchange with cryptographic consensus and swarm-based parallel probing.","zh":"赋予代理设计和评估分布式系统的能力，使用Paxos一致性协议和TLA+正式规范，确保可靠和安全的数据交换，使用加密一致性协议和基于集群的并行探测。","ja":"PaxosコンセンサスプロトコルとTLA+形式仕様を使用して、分散システムを設計し評価する代理の能力を与え、暗号コンセンサスプロトコルとスウォームベースの並列プローブを使用して、信頼性の高いセキュアなデータ交換を実現します。","ko":"Paxos 합의 프로토콜과 TLA+ 형식 사양을 사용하여 분산 시스템을 설계 및 평가할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하고, 암호화 합의 프로토콜 및 스ウォーム 기반의 병렬 프로브를 사용하여 신뢰할 수 있는 보안 데이터 교환을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar y evaluar sistemas distribuidos utilizando el consenso Paxos y la especificación formal TLA+, garantizando un intercambio de datos confiable y seguro con consenso criptográfico y sondeo paralelo basado en enjambre.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et d''évaluer des systèmes distribués en utilisant le consensus Paxos et la spécification formelle TLA+, garantissant un échange de données fiable et sécurisé avec un consensus cryptographique et une exploration parallèle basée sur l''essaim.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, verteilte Systeme mit Paxos-Konsens und TLA+-Formalspezifikation zu entwerfen und zu bewerten, wodurch ein zuverlässiger und sicherer Datenaustausch mit kryptografischem Konsens und schwarmbasierter paralleler Prüfung gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar e avaliar sistemas distribuídos usando o consenso Paxos e a especificação formal TLA+, garantindo a troca de dados confiável e segura com o consenso criptográfico e a sondagem paralela baseada em enxame.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разрабатывать и оценивать распределенные системы с использованием согласования Paxos и формальной спецификации TLA+, обеспечивая надежный и безопасный обмен данными с криптографическим согласованием и параллельным зондированием на основе роя.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تصميم وتقييم أنظمة موزعة باستخدام إجماع Paxos والمواصفة الرسمية TLA+، مما يضمن تبادل البيانات الموثوق والآمن مع الإجماع التشفيري والاستكشاف الموازي المستند إلى السرب."},"useCases":{"en":["Evaluating distributed adversarial behavioral security","Implementing fault-tolerant systems with logical clocks","Developing scalable consensus protocols using Paxos"],"zh":["评估分布式对抗行为安全性","使用逻辑时钟实现容错系统","使用Paxos开发可扩展的合意协议"],"ja":["分散アドバーサリアル行動のセキュリティを評価する","論理時計を使用して障害耐性システムを実装する","Paxosを使用してスケーラブルなコンセンサスプロトコルを開発する"],"ko":["분산 적대적 행동 보안性 평가","논리 시계를 사용하여 오류 제어 시스템 구현","Paxos를 사용하여 확장 가능한 합의 프로토콜 개발"],"es":["Evaluación de seguridad del comportamiento adversario distribuido","Implementación de sistemas tolerantes a fallos con relojes lógicos","Desarrollo de protocolos de consenso escalables utilizando Paxos"],"fr":["Évaluation de la sécurité des comportements adversariaux distribués","Mise en œuvre de systèmes tolérants aux pannes avec horloges logiques","Développement de protocoles de consensus évolutifs utilisant Paxos"],"de":["Bewertung der Sicherheit von verteiltem adversarischem Verhalten","Implementierung von fehlertoleranten Systemen mit logischen Uhren","Entwicklung skalierbarer Konsensprotokolle mit Paxos"],"pt":["Avaliar a segurança comportamental adversária distribuída","Implementar sistemas tolerantes a falhas com relógios lógicos","Desenvolver protocolos de consenso escaláveis usando Paxos"],"ru":["Оценка распределенной безопасной поведенческой системы","Реализация систем с устойчивостью к отказам и логическими часами","Разработка масштабируемых протоколов согласования с использованием Paxos"],"ar":["تقييم أمن السلوك الموزع المعادي","تنفيذ أنظمة متسامحة على الأعطال بساعات منطقية","تطوير بروتوكولات إجماع قابلة للتوسعة باستخدام Paxos"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of distributed system fundamentals","Limited to systems that can implement TLA+ and Paxos","Dependent on cryptographic consensus protocols for security"],"zh":["需要理解分布式系统的基础知识","仅限于可以实现TLA+和Paxos的系统","依赖于加密一致性协议以实现安全性"],"ja":["分散システムの基礎知識を理解する必要がある","TLA+とPaxosを実装できるシステムのみに限定される","セキュリティを実現するために暗号コンセンサスプロトコルに依存する"],"ko":["분산 시스템의 기본 지식을 이해해야 함","TLA+ 및 Paxos를 구현할 수 있는 시스템에만 제한됨","보안을 구현하기 위해 암호화 합의 프로토콜에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los fundamentos de los sistemas distribuidos","Limitado a sistemas que pueden implementar TLA+ y Paxos","Dependiente de protocolos de consenso criptográfico para la seguridad"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des fondamentaux des systèmes distribués","Limité aux systèmes pouvant implémenter TLA+ et Paxos","Dépendant des protocoles de consensus cryptographique pour la sécurité"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis der Grundlagen verteilter Systeme","Beschränkt auf Systeme, die TLA+ und Paxos implementieren können","Abhängig von kryptografischen Konsensprotokollen für die Sicherheit"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos fundamentos dos sistemas distribuídos","Limitado a sistemas que possam implementar TLA+ e Paxos","Dependente de protocolos de consenso criptográficos para segurança"],"ru":["Требует понимания основ распределенных систем","Ограничен системами, которые могут реализовать TLA+ и Paxos","Зависит от криптографических протоколов согласования для безопасности"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم أساسيات أنظمة الموزعة","محدود لأنظمة يمكنها تنفيذ TLA+ وPaxos","يعتمد على بروتوكولات الإجماع التشفيرية للأمان"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d28266b0ddc083a8014f21ed34c4c3995e8bf60b6940fa80ce9af2e076b5f27e","qualityScore":36}');
