и Node.js","Интерфейс командной строки (CLI) для простого управления"],"ar":["تصحيح الأخطاء في الكود باستخدام تتبع المهام beads","تحسين المهام بقدرات فائقة من Claude Code","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Python و Node.js","واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) للتحكم السهل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用AI工具调试","什么是AI工具","AI工具替代品","AI工具与竞争对手的比较","AI工具安装","AI工具设置指南","代码调试最佳实践","AI工具集成"],"ja":["AIエージェントの使用方法","AIエージェントとは","AIエージェントの代替品","AIエージェントと競合製品の比較","AIエージェントのインストール","AIエージェントの設定ガイド","コードデバッグのベストプラクティス","AIエージェントの統合"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 사용 방법","AI 에이전트란","AI 에이전트 대안","AI 에이전트와 경쟁사 비교","AI 에이전트 설치","AI 에이전트 설정 가이드","코드 디버깅 베스트 프랙티스","AI 에이전트 통합"],"es":["cómo usar herramientas de AI","qué es la depuración con AI","Claude Code alternativa","Claude Code vs otros","instalar Claude Code","guía de configuración de Claude Code","herramientas de depuración de AI","desarrollo con AI"],"fr":["comment utiliser des outils d''IA","qu''est-ce que le débogage avec l''IA","alternative à Claude Code","Claude Code vs autres","installer Claude Code","guide de configuration de Claude Code","outils de débogage d''IA","développement avec l''IA"],"de":["wie man AI-Tools verwendet","was ist Debugging mit AI","Alternative zu Claude Code","Claude Code vs andere","Claude Code installieren","Einrichtungsanleitung für Claude Code","AI-Debugging-Tools","Entwicklung mit AI"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de depuração","o que é depuração de código","alternativa para Claude Code","Claude Code vs outras ferramentas","instalar Claude Code","guia de configuração do Claude Code","depuração de código em Python","depuração de código em Node.js"],"ru":["как использовать инструменты отладки","что такое отладка кода","альтернатива Claude Code","Claude Code vs другие инструменты","установить Claude Code","руководство по настройке Claude Code","отладка кода на Python","отладка кода на Node.js"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات تصحيح الأخطاء","ما هو تصحيح الأخطاء في الكود","بديل ل Claude Code","Claude Code مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت Claude Code","دليل إعداد Claude Code","تصحيح الأخطاء في الكود بال파이썬","تصحيح الأخطاء في الكود بنود.جس"]}},"owner":"withzombies","repo":"hyperpowers","repoPath":"withzombies/hyperpowers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.923Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"debugging-with-tools","description":"Use when encountering bugs or test failures - systematic debugging using debuggers, internet research, and agents to find root cause before fixing","bodyPreview":"<codex_compat>\nThis skill was ported from Claude Code. In Codex:\n- \"Skill tool\" means read the skill''s `SKILL.md` from disk.\n- \"TodoWrite\" means create and maintain a checklist section in your response.\n- \"Task()\" means `spawn_agent` (dispatch in parallel via `multi_tool_use.parallel` when needed).\n- Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not available; skip those steps.\n</codex_compat>\n\n\n<skill_overview>\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Always use tools to understand root caus","body":"<codex_compat>\nThis skill was ported from Claude Code. In Codex:\n- \"Skill tool\" means read the skill''s `SKILL.md` from disk.\n- \"TodoWrite\" means create and maintain a checklist section in your response.\n- \"Task()\" means `spawn_agent` (dispatch in parallel via `multi_tool_use.parallel` when needed).\n- Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not available; skip those steps.\n</codex_compat>\n\n\n<skill_overview>\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Always use tools to understand root cause BEFORE attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n</skill_overview>\n\n<rigidity_level>\nMEDIUM FREEDOM - Must complete investigation phases (tools → hypothesis → test) before fixing.\n\nCan adapt tool choice to language/context. Never skip investigation or guess at fixes.\n</rigidity_level>\n\n<quick_reference>\n\n| Phase | Tools to Use | Output |\n|-------|--------------|--------|\n| **1. Investigate** | Error messages, internet-researcher agent, debugger, codebase-investigator | Root cause understanding |\n| **2. Hypothesize** | Form theory based on evidence (not guesses) | Testable hypothesis |\n| **3. Test** | Validate hypothesis with minimal change | Confirms or rejects theory |\n| **4. Fix** | Implement proper fix for root cause | Problem solved permanently |\n\n**FORBIDDEN:** Skip investigation → guess at fix → hope it works\n**REQUIRED:** Tools → evidence → hypothesis → test → fix\n\n**Key agents:**\n- `internet-researcher` - Search error messages, known bugs, solutions\n- `codebase-investigator` - Understand code structure, find related code\n- `test-runner` - Run tests without output pollution\n\n</quick_reference>\n\n<when_to_use>\n**Use for ANY technical issue:**\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production or development\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n- Performance problems\n\n**ESPECIALLY when:**\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- Error message is unclear\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n</when_to_use>\n\n<the_process>\n\n## Phase 1: Tool-Assisted Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix, gather evidence with tools:**\n\n### 1. Read Complete Error Messages\n\n- Entire error message (not just first line)\n- Complete stack trace (all frames)\n- Line numbers, file paths, error codes\n- Stack traces show exact execution path\n\n### 2. Search Internet FIRST (Use internet-researcher Agent)\n\n**Dispatch internet-researcher with:**\n```\n\"Search for error: [exact error message]\n- Check Stack Overflow solutions\n- Look for GitHub issues in [library] version [X]\n- Find official documentation explaining this error\n- Check if this is a known bug\"\n```\n\n**What agent should find:**\n- Exact matches to your error\n- Similar symptoms and solutions\n- Known bugs in your dependency versions\n- Workarounds that worked for others\n\n### 3. Use Debugger to Inspect State\n\n**Claude cannot run debuggers directly. Instead:**\n\n**Option A - Recommend debugger to user:**\n```\n\"Let''s use lldb/gdb/DevTools to inspect state at error location.\nPlease run: [specific commands]\nWhen breakpoint hits: [what to inspect]\nShare output with me.\"\n```\n\n**Option B - Add instrumentation Claude can add:**\n```rust\n// Add logging\nprintln!(\"DEBUG: var = {:?}, state = {:?}\", var, state);\n\n// Add assertions\nassert!(condition, \"Expected X but got {:?}\", actual);\n```\n\n### 4. Investigate Codebase (Use codebase-investigator Agent)\n\n**Dispatch codebase-investigator with:**\n```\n\"Error occurs in function X at line Y.\nFind:\n- How is X called? What are the callers?\n- What does variable Z contain at this point?\n- Are there similar functions that work correctly?\n- What changed recently in this area?\"\n```\n\n## Phase 2: Form Hypothesis\n\n**Based on evidence (not guesses):**\n\n1. **State what you know** (from investigation)\n2. **Propose theory** explaining the evidence\n3. **Make prediction** that tests the theory\n\n**Example:**\n```\nKnown: Error \"null pointer\" at auth.rs:45 when email is empty\nTheory: Empty email bypasses validation, passes null to login()\nPrediction: Adding validation before login() will prevent error\nTest: Add validation, verify error doesn''t occur with empty email\n```\n\n**NEVER:**\n- Guess without evidence\n- Propose fix without hypothesis\n- Skip to \"try this and see\"\n\n## Phase 3: Test Hypothesis\n\n**Minimal change to validate theory:**\n\n1. Make smallest change that tests hypothesis\n2. Run test/reproduction case\n3. Observe result\n\n**If confirmed:** Proceed to Phase 4\n**If rejected:** Return to Phase 1 with new information\n\n## Phase 4: Implement Fix\n\n**After understanding root cause:**\n\n1. Write test reproducing bug (RED phase - use test-driven-development skill)\n2. Implement proper fix addressing root cause\n3. Verify test passes (GREEN phase)\n4. Run full test suite (regression check)\n5. Commit fix\n\n**The fix should:**\n- Address root cause (not symptom)\n- Be minimal and focused\n- Include test preventing regression\n\n</the_process>\n\n<examples>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer encounters test failure, immediately tries \"obvious\" fix without investigation</scenario>\n\n<code>\nTest error:\n```\nFAIL: test_login_expired_token\nAssertionError: Expected Err(TokenExpired), got Ok(User)\n```\n\nDeveloper thinks: \"Obviously the token expiration check is wrong\"\n\nMakes change without investigation:\n```rust\n// \"Fix\" - just check if token is expired\nif token.expires_at < now() {\n    return Err(AuthError::TokenExpired);\n}\n```\n\nCommits without testing other cases.\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n**No investigation:**\n- Didn''t read error completely\n- Didn''t check what `expires_at` contains\n- Didn''t debug to see token state\n- Didn''t search for similar issues\n\n**What actually happened:** Token `expires_at` was being parsed incorrectly, always showing future date. The \"fix\" adds dead code that never runs.\n\n**Result:** Bug not fixed, new dead code added, time wasted.\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Phase 1 - Investigate with tools:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Read complete error\nFAIL: test_login_expired_token at line 45\nExpected: Err(TokenExpired)\nGot: Ok(User { id: 123 })\nToken: { expires_at: \"2099-01-01\", ... }\n```\n\n**Dispatch internet-researcher:**\n```\n\"Search for: token expiration always showing future date\n- Check date parsing bugs\n- Look for timezone issues\n- Find JWT expiration handling\"\n```\n\n**Add instrumentation:**\n```rust\nprintln!(\"DEBUG: expires_at = {:?}, now = {:?}, expired = {:?}\",\n         token.expires_at, now(), token.expires_at < now());\n```\n\n**Run test again:**\n```\nDEBUG: expires_at = 2099-01-01T00:00:00Z, now = 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z, expired = false\n```\n\n**Phase 2 - Hypothesis:**\n\"Token `expires_at` is being set to 2099, not actual expiration. Problem is in token creation, not validation.\"\n\n**Phase 3 - Test:**\nCheck token creation code:\n```rust\n// Found the bug!\nfn create_token() -> Token {\n    Token {\n        expires_at: \"2099-01-01\".parse()?, // HARDCODED!\n        ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Phase 4 - Fix root cause:**\n```rust\nfn create_token(duration: Duration) -> Token {\n    Token {\n        expires_at: now() + duration,  // Correct\n        ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Result:** Root cause fixed, test passes, no dead code.\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer skips internet search, reinvents solution to known problem</scenario>\n\n<code>\nError:\n```\nerror: linking with `cc` failed: exit status: 1\nld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64\n```\n\nDeveloper thinks: \"Must be a linking issue, I''ll add flags\"\n\nSpends 2 hours trying different linker flags:\n```toml\n[target.aarch64-apple-darwin]\nrustflags = [\"-C\", \"link-arg=-undefined dynamic_lookup\"]\n# Doesn''t work, tries more flags...\n```\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n**Skipped internet search:**\n- This is a common error with known solutions\n- Stack Overflow has exact fix\n- Official docs explain the issue\n- Wasted 2 hours reinventing solution\n\n**Why it happens:** Impatience, thinking \"I can figure this out faster\"\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Dispatch internet-researcher FIRST:**\n\n```\n\"Search for: ''symbol not found for architecture arm64'' Rust linking\n- Check Stack Overflow solutions\n- Look for Xcode/macOS specific fixes\n- Find Cargo configuration for Apple Silicon\"\n```\n\n**Agent returns (30 seconds):**\n```\nFound on Stack Overflow (2.4k upvotes):\nThis occurs when Xcode Command Line Tools aren''t installed or outdated.\n\nSolution:\nxcode-select --install\n\nOr update existing:\nsoftwareupdate --all --install --force\n```\n\n**Apply solution:**\n```bash\nxcode-select --install\n# Wait for installation\ncargo build\n# Success!\n```\n\n**Result:** Fixed in 5 minutes, not 2 hours.\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer fixes symptom without understanding root cause, bug returns different way</scenario>\n\n<code>\nBug: Users can delete other users'' posts\n\nDeveloper notices: DELETE /posts/:id doesn''t check ownership\n\n\"Fix\":\n```python\n@app.delete(\"/posts/{post_id}\")\ndef delete_post(post_id: int, user: User):\n    post = get_post(post_id)\n    if post.author_id != user.id:\n        raise Forbidden()\n    delete(post)\n```\n\nBug \"fixed\"... but bug report comes back: \"Users can edit other users'' posts\"\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n**Symptom fix:**\n- Fixed DELETE endpoint\n- Didn''t investigate root cause\n- Didn''t check other endpoints\n\n**Root cause:** No authorization middleware checking ownership across ALL endpoints.\n\n**Result:** Whack-a-mole fixing symptoms, not the underlying issue.\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Phase 1 - Investigate with codebase-investigator:**\n\n```\n\"User can delete other users'' posts. Investigate:\n- What authorization exists across all post endpoints?\n- Is there a pattern for ownership checks?\n- Which other endpoints access posts?\n- Is there middleware handling this?\"\n```\n\n**Agent reports:**\n```\nFound:\n- DELETE /posts/:id - NO ownership check\n- PUT /posts/:id - NO ownership check\n- GET /posts/:id - NO ownership check (allows viewing private posts!)\n- No authorization middleware found\n- Similar pattern in comments, likes endpoints\n```\n\n**Phase 2 - Hypothesis:**\n\"Missing authorization layer. Need middleware checking resource ownership across ALL endpoints.\"\n\n**Phase 4 - Fix root cause:**\n```python\n# Add authorization middleware\nclass OwnershipMiddleware:\n    def check_ownership(self, resource, user):\n        if resource.author_id != user.id:\n            raise Forbidden()\n\n# Apply to all endpoints\n@app.delete(\"/posts/{post_id}\")\n@require_ownership(Post)\ndef delete_post(...):\n    ...\n\n@app.put(\"/posts/{post_id}\")\n@require_ownership(Post)\ndef update_post(...):\n    ...\n```\n\n**Result:** Root cause fixed, ALL endpoints secured, not just one symptom.\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n</examples>\n\n<critical_rules>\n\n## Rules That Have No Exceptions\n\n1. **Tools before fixes** → Never guess without investigation\n   - Use internet-researcher for errors\n   - Use debugger or instrumentation for state\n   - Use codebase-investigator for context\n\n2. **Evidence-based hypotheses** → Not guesses or hunches\n   - State what tools revealed\n   - Propose theory explaining evidence\n   - Make testable prediction\n\n3. **Test hypothesis before fixing** → Minimal change to validate\n   - Smallest change that tests theory\n   - Observe result\n   - If wrong, return to investigation\n\n4. **Fix root cause, not symptom** → One fix, many symptoms prevented\n   - Understand why problem occurred\n   - Fix the underlying issue\n   - Don''t play whack-a-mole\n\n## Common Excuses\n\nAll of these mean: Stop, use tools to investigate:\n- \"The fix is obvious\"\n- \"I know what this is\"\n- \"Just a quick try\"\n- \"No time for debugging\"\n- \"Error message is clear enough\"\n- \"Internet search will take too long\"\n\n</critical_rules>\n\n<verification_checklist>\n\nBefore proposing any fix:\n- [ ] Read complete error message (not just first line)\n- [ ] Dispatched internet-researcher for unclear errors\n- [ ] Used debugger or added instrumentation to inspect state\n- [ ] Dispatched codebase-investigator to understand context\n- [ ] Formed hypothesis based on evidence (not guesses)\n- [ ] Tested hypothesis with minimal change\n- [ ] Verified hypothesis confirmed before fixing\n\nBefore committing fix:\n- [ ] Written test reproducing bug (RED phase)\n- [ ] Verified test fails before fix\n- [ ] Implemented fix addressing root cause\n- [ ] Verified test passes after fix (GREEN phase)\n- [ ] Ran full test suite (regression check)\n\n</verification_checklist>\n\n<integration>\n\n**This skill calls:**\n- internet-researcher (search errors, known bugs, solutions)\n- codebase-investigator (understand code structure, find related code)\n- test-driven-development (write test for bug, implement fix)\n- test-runner (run tests without output pollution)\n\n**This skill is called by:**\n- fixing-bugs (complete bug fix workflow)\n- root-cause-tracing (deep debugging for complex issues)\n- Any skill when encountering unexpected behavior\n\n**Agents used:**\n- hyperpowers:internet-researcher (search for error solutions)\n- hyperpowers:codebase-investigator (understand codebase context)\n- hyperpowers:test-runner (run tests, return summary only)\n\n</integration>\n\n<resources>\n\n**Detailed guides:**\n- [Debugger reference](resources/debugger-reference.md) - LLDB, GDB, DevTools commands\n- [Debugging session example](resources/debugging-session-example.md) - Complete walkthrough\n\n**When stuck:**\n- Error unclear → Dispatch internet-researcher with exact error text\n- Don''t understand code flow → Dispatch codebase-investigator\n- Need to inspect runtime state → Recommend debugger to user or add instrumentation\n- Tempted to guess → Stop, use tools to gather evidence first\n\n</resources>"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:26:25.948Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing systematic bug resolution with tool-based root cause analysis.","zh":"非常适合需要系统性错误解决和基于工具的根本原因分析的开发Agent。","ja":"ツールベースの根本原因分析による体系的なバグ解決を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"도구 기반의 근본 원인 분석을 통한 체계적인 버그 해결이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una resolución sistemática de errores con análisis de causa raíz basado en herramientas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une résolution systématique des bogues avec une analyse de cause racine basée sur les outils.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine systematische Fehlerbehebung mit toolbasierter Root Cause-Analyse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de resolução sistemática de bugs com análise de causa raiz baseada em ferramentas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуется систематическое решение проблем с помощью инструментального анализа коренной причины.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيين الذين يحتاجون إلى حل منهجي للأخطاء مع تحليل السبب الأصلي القائم على الأداة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to methodically debug code using tools like task tracking and refinement, streamlining the process with parallel dispatch via multi_tool_use.parallel and leveraging checklist sections for TodoWrite functionality.","zh":"使Agent能够使用方法论调试代码，使用诸如任务跟踪和优化等工具，通过multi_tool_use.parallel进行并行分派以简化流程，并利用清单部分实现TodoWrite功能。","ja":"タスク追跡と改良などのツールを使用して、エージェントが体系的な方法でコードをデバッグできるようにし、multi_tool_use.parallelによる並列ディスパッチでプロセスを合理化し、チェックリストセクションを活用してTodoWrite機能を実現します。","ko":"작업 추적 및 개선과 같은 도구를 사용하여 에이전트가 체계적으로 코드를 디버깅할 수 있도록 하고, multi_tool_use.parallel을 통한 병렬 디스패치로 프로세스를 간소화하며, 체크리스트 섹션을 활용하여 TodoWrite 기능을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a depurar el código de manera metódica utilizando herramientas como seguimiento de tareas y refinamiento, simplificando el proceso con despacho paralelo a través de multi_tool_use.parallel y aprovechando secciones de lista de verificación para la funcionalidad de TodoWrite.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déboguer le code de manière méthodique en utilisant des outils tels que le suivi des tâches et le raffinement, en simplifiant le processus avec un dispatch parallèle via multi_tool_use.parallel et en exploitant les sections de liste de vérification pour la fonctionnalité TodoWrite.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, den Code methodisch zu debuggen, indem sie Tools wie Aufgabenverfolgung und Verfeinerung verwenden, wodurch der Prozess durch parallelen Dispatch über multi_tool_use.parallel gestreamlined und die Checklistensektionen für die TodoWrite-Funktionalität genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a depurar metodicamente o código usando ferramentas como rastreamento de tarefas e refinamento, otimizando o processo com despacho paralelo via multi_tool_use.parallel e aproveitando seções de lista de verificação para funcionalidade TodoWrite.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью методически отлаживать код, используя инструменты, такие как отслеживание задач и уточнение, оптимизируя процесс с помощью параллельной отправки через multi_tool_use.parallel и используя разделы контрольных списков для функциональности TodoWrite.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصحيح الأخطاء بطريقة منهجية باستخدام أدوات مثل تتبع المهام وتحسينها ، وتبسيط العملية باستخدام الإرسال الموازي عبر multi_tool_use.parallel وتحقيق أقسام قائمة التحقق من الوظيفة TodoWrite."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex codebases with systematic tool-based approaches","Refining task tracking for efficient bug resolution","Utilizing parallel dispatch for accelerated debugging"],"zh":["使用系统化的基于工具的方法调试复杂的代码库","优化任务跟踪以实现高效的错误解决","利用并行分派来加速调试过程"],"ja":["体系的なツールベースのアプローチを使用した複雑なコードベースのデバッグ","効率的なバグ解決のためのタスク追跡の改良","加速されたデバッグのための並列ディス패ッチの利用"],"ko":["체계적인 도구 기반 접근법으로 복잡한 코드베이스 디버깅","효율적인 버그 해결을 위한 작업 추적 개선","가속화된 디버깅을 위한 병렬 디스패치 활용"],"es":["Depuración de bases de código complejas con enfoques sistemáticos basados en herramientas","Refinamiento del seguimiento de tareas para una resolución eficiente de errores","Utilización de despacho paralelo para una depuración acelerada"],"fr":["Débogage de bases de code complexes avec des approches systématiques basées sur les outils","Raffinement du suivi des tâches pour une résolution efficace des bogues","Utilisation d''un dispatch parallèle pour un débogage accéléré"],"de":["Fehlersuche in komplexen Codebasen mit toolbasierten Ansätzen","Verfeinerung der Aufgabenverfolgung für eine effiziente Fehlerbehebung","Nutzung von parallelem Dispatch für eine beschleunigte Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Depuração de bases de código complexas com abordagens sistemáticas baseadas em ferramentas","Refinamento do rastreamento de tarefas para resolução eficiente de bugs","Utilização de despacho paralelo para depuração acelerada"],"ru":["Отладка сложных кодовых баз с помощью системных инструментальных подходов","Уточнение отслеживания задач для эффективного решения проблем","Использование параллельной отправки для ускоренной отладки"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء قواعد التعليمات البرمجية المعقدة باستخدام نهج منهجي قائم على الأداة","تحسين تتبع المهام لحل الأخطاء بكفاءة","استخدام الإرسال الموازي لتصحيح الأخطاء المتسارع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Codex compatibility for skill tool functionality","Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not supported"],"zh":["需要Codex兼容性以实现技能工具功能","不支持Claude特定的钩子和斜杠命令"],"ja":["スキルツール機能にはCodex互換性が必要","Claude固有のフックとスラッシュコマンドはサポートされていない"],"ko":["스킬 도구 기능을 위해 Codex 호환성 필요","Claude 특정 훅 및 슬래시 명령어는 지원되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Codex para la funcionalidad de herramientas de habilidad","No se admiten ganchos ni comandos de barra específicos de Claude"],"fr":["Nécessite une compatibilité avec Codex pour la fonctionnalité des outils de compétence","Les crochets et les commandes de barre spécifiques à Claude ne sont pas pris en charge"],"de":["Benötigt Codex-Kompatibilität für die Funktionalität von Skill-Tools","Claude-spezifische Hooks und Slash-Befehle werden nicht unterstützt"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com Codex para funcionalidade da ferramenta de habilidade","Ganchos e comandos de barra específicos do Claude não são suportados"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с Codex для функциональности инструмента навыка","Крючки и команды слэша, специфичные для Claude, не поддерживаются"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع Codex لتوظيف أداة المهارة","أدوات ورسائل الشرطة الخاصة ب Claude غير مدعومة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d3980914f5dc48666cf345e9a6cb56d90edda5c7d774f9c7fdfc3c0e6599ef31","qualityScore":34}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('scotttrinh/nook/effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks', 'community', 'scotttrinh', 'nook', 'scotttrinh/nook', 'effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks', 0, 0, 34, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.926Z', '2026-03-02T02:28:19.632Z', '2a13914b47db688bdd1705a78a6ed6d1965f35c90a558f8e3a46471f76e1d295', '{"id":"scotttrinh/nook/effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks","name":"effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks","description":{"zh":"NixOS模块为隔离工作树容器提供周期任务调度功能","ja":"NixOSモジュールは隔離されたワークツリーコンテナ用の周期タスクのスケジューリング機能を提供します","ko":"NixOS 모듈은 분리된 워크트리 컨테이너를 위한 주기적 작업 스케줄링 기능을 제공합니다","es":"El módulo NixOS para contenedores de worktree aislados permite la programación de tareas periódicas de manera efectiva","fr":"Le module NixOS pour les conteneurs de worktree isolés permet la planification de tâches périodiques de manière efficace","de":"Das NixOS-Modul für isolierte Worktree-Container ermöglicht die effektive Planung von periodischen Aufgaben","pt":"O módulo NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks permite a criação de contêineres de worktree isolados para agendar tarefas periódicas de forma eficiente","ru":"Модуль NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks позволяет создавать изолированные контейнеры worktree для планирования периодических задач эффективно","ar":"الوحدة NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks تمكن من إنشاء تحتويز worktree معزولة لجدولة المهام الدورية بفعالية","en":"NixOS Module for isolated worktree containers"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理-周期任务调度模式","ja":"AIエージェント-周期タスクのスケジューリングパターン","ko":"AI 에이전트-주기적 작업 스케줄링 패턴","es":"Herramientas de IA: Patrones de Efecto para Tareas Periód...","fr":"Outils IA : Modèle d''Effet pour Tâches Périodiques","de":"KI-Tools: Effektmuster für Periodische Aufgaben","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks","ru":"ИИ Агенты: effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: effect-patterns-scheduling-period...","en":"effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks"},"description":{"zh":"NixOS模块为隔离工作树容器提供周期任务调度功能","ja":"NixOSモジュールは隔離されたワークツリーコンテナ用の周期タスクのスケジューリング機能を提供します","ko":"NixOS 모듈은 분리된 워크트리 컨테이너를 위한 주기적 작업 스케줄링 기능을 제공합니다","es":"El módulo NixOS para contenedores de worktree aislados permite la programación de tareas periódicas de manera efectiva","fr":"Le module NixOS pour les conteneurs de worktree isolés permet la planification de tâches périodiques de manière efficace","de":"Das NixOS-Modul für isolierte Worktree-Container ermöglicht die effektive Planung von periodischen Aufgaben","pt":"O módulo NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks permite a criação de contêineres de worktree isolados para agendar tarefas periódicas de forma efici...","ru":"Модуль NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks позволяет создавать изолированные контейнеры worktree для планирования периодических задач эффективно","ar":"الوحدة NixOS effect-patterns-scheduling-periodic-tasks تمكن من إنشاء تحتويز worktree معزولة لجدولة المهام الدورية بفعالية","en":"NixOS Module for isolated worktree containers"},"definition":{"en":"NixOS Module for isolated worktree containers"},"features":{"zh":["隔离工作树容器","周期任务调度","NixOS模块支持","简化任务管理","提高系统稳定性"],"ja":["隔離されたワークツリーコンテナ","周期タスクのスケジューリング","NixOSモジュールのサポート","タスク管理の簡素化","システムの安定性の向上"],"ko":["분리된 워크트리 컨테이너","주기적 작업 스케줄링","NixOS 모듈 지원","작업 관리의 단순화","시스템 안정性的 향상"],"es":["Programación de tareas periódicas","Contenedores de worktree aislados","Integración con NixOS","Ejecución de tareas de manera efectiva","Seguridad mejorada mediante aislamiento"],"fr":["Planification de tâches périodiques","Conteneurs de worktree isolés","Intégration avec NixOS","Exécution de tâches de manière efficace","Sécurité améliorée grâce à l''isolement"],"de":["Planung von periodischen Aufgaben","Isolierte Worktree-Container","Integration mit NixOS","Ausführung von Aufgaben in e